1
00:00:00,830 --> 00:00:05,180
A timeline is a line of time.
Earlier is on the left,

2
00:00:05,230 --> 00:00:09,410
later on the right, and the ruler along
the line tells you where you are,

3
00:00:09,460 --> 00:00:12,349
whether that's years, days or seconds.

4
00:00:13,779 --> 00:00:18,169
A dot is a moment: one point
in time, with its title.

5
00:00:18,219 --> 00:00:22,689
A band is a duration: a stretch
with a start and an end.

6
00:00:22,739 --> 00:00:27,459
A dot with a number is a summary: moments
too close together to draw apart at

7
00:00:27,509 --> 00:00:32,419
this zoom, and the number says how
many. And an arc above the line is a

8
00:00:32,469 --> 00:00:36,336
relationship, linking two
things that are connected.

9
00:00:37,766 --> 00:00:43,106
To zoom, scroll, or pinch with
two fingers side by side.

10
00:00:43,156 --> 00:00:47,866
Zoom in on a summary and it opens
up into the moments inside it.

11
00:00:47,916 --> 00:00:52,166
Drag to move along the line,
or up and down. On a keyboard,

12
00:00:52,216 --> 00:00:55,223
the arrow keys pan and
plus and minus zoom.

13
00:00:56,763 --> 00:01:01,683
Lost? Fit all shows the
whole timeline again.

14
00:01:01,733 --> 00:01:06,963
Search, or the slash key, finds moments
by their words and takes you there.

15
00:01:07,013 --> 00:01:10,373
Full screen, or F, gives the
timeline the whole window,

16
00:01:10,423 --> 00:01:12,846
and Escape brings the page back.

17
00:01:14,566 --> 00:01:17,816
Click or tap a moment or a
band to read it: its pictures,

18
00:01:17,866 --> 00:01:22,636
its time, its tags, its notes,
and what it's related to.

19
00:01:22,686 --> 00:01:26,526
Choose a related item to read
that one next. On a phone,

20
00:01:26,576 --> 00:01:29,502
the reader fills the screen.

21
00:01:31,162 --> 00:01:34,452
Separate by tags pulls one
thread, like every storm,

22
00:01:34,502 --> 00:01:40,032
into a track of its own; Rejoin puts
it back. And a timeline's time display

23
00:01:40,082 --> 00:01:45,837
decides how its times read: as dates,
as years, or as exact numbers.

24
00:01:47,537 --> 00:01:52,187
That's all it takes to read any
timeline. Open a public one,

25
00:01:52,237 --> 00:01:54,534
no account needed, and look around.
